  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_012, acc=0.725) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer aggregation + weighted fusion in multiprofile mode. All top performers share these two encoders, and transformer aggregation clearly outperforms avgpool (0.725 vs 0.706). However, no singleprofile configuration has been tested with this best encoder pair. Question: config_009 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, singleprofile, weighted) tests whether removing the multiprofile aggregation step (aggregation=None) could be competitive or even superior, since singleprofile avoids potential information loss from averaging/transformer pooling across profiles. Why this is the best use: With only 1 experiment remaining after this, I need the highest-information experiment. Singleprofile is the only major architectural axis untested with the best encoders. If it matches or beats 0.725, it opens a new direction for the final experiment; if it underperforms, it firmly confirms multiprofile+transformer as optimal and lets the last experiment focus on fine-tuning (e.g., testing a minor fusion variant). This maximizes expected value under the tight budget."
}

